{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01Yadn6fLkNZb2RVCQ2G9WMT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. **Q15 — Partial observability or missing information?** is written and committed.\n\n**What the note covers:**\n\n- **Classify-by-type framework** — six distinct scenarios (ambiguous intent, empty tool result, tool error/timeout, conflicting outputs, incomplete observation, stale context) each with its own mitigation, not a one-size-fits-all retry.\n- **Structured `MISSING_INFO` action type** — the LLM emits a typed ReAct action when it detects missing data; the orchestrator catches it deterministically rather than parsing error prose.\n- **Proportional response ladder** — empty result → retry with query rewriting (HyDE/BM25 fallback); ambiguous intent → single clarifying question; critical gap on irreversible action → checkpoint + LangGraph `interrupt_before` HITL.\n- **Key pitfall called out:** letting the LLM decide what to do on a tool error (parsing failure prose) vs. structured `status` fields that let the orchestrator branch deterministically.\n\nNext up in the queue: **Q16 — How agents decide a task is \"done\"?**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":345,"cache_read_input_tokens":62916,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":345,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71f9ab34-4a45-40d2-a740-9d7c088f3691","uuid":"ce88966d-d8c7-4097-b661-45d4365b398f"}
